# Nissan Cherry N12 three-door hatchback, 1982-1986.
#
# The angular 1982-86 Cherry, a size larger than the N10 and the model that sat
# alongside the new Micra in the Nissan range. Sold in Britain as the Datsun
# Cherry and then the Nissan Cherry; in Japan and Australia it was the Pulsar,
# and in Italy it was built as the Alfa Romeo Arna. The three-door hatchback is
# modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Cherry
#
# Dimensions 3.960 x 1.620 x 1.390 m, wheelbase 2.415 m, from the English
# Wikipedia Pulsar N12 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to
# 1.827 m; projecting front indicators take the length to 3.961 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the N12 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: red, white, blue and silver. Weights red 3, white 3, blue 2,
# silver 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 155 km/h for the 1.3, the volume UK engine. Comfort 65/280, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 65, a step above the N10's 55/265 because the N12 is a larger,
# better-riding car. Classes 0,1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: September 1982 intro, retires staggered 1997-2000 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-n12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-cherry-n12.dae (53 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-cherry-n12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# At 128 px the angular N12 nose, the long single door with its triangular
# quarter glass and the sloping hatch read correctly.

